ating system: Docker image\r\n- Database (use `[x]`):\r\n  - [x] PostgreSQL\r\n  - [ ] MySQL\r\n  - [x] SQLite\r\n- Can you reproduce the bug at https://try.gitea.io:\r\n  - [ ] Yes (provide example URL)\r\n  - [ ] No\r\n  - [x] Not relevant\r\n- Log gist: https://gist.github.com/mjwwit/08966dde2b08b4ecd941112c3c754d8a\r\n\r\n## Description\r\nThe error in the gist linked above takes place when trying to create a repository after migrating from a sqlite3 database to a postgres database using `gitea dump`.\r\nThe issue is that the sequences aren't set to correct values in the dump. This means that they all start at `0`. Any insertions get the next sequence number, `1`, which is most likely already taken, causing the conflict.","closed_by":{"login":"bkcsoft","id":4726179,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MjYxNzk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4726179?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkcsoft","html_url":"https://github.com/bkcsoft","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkcsoft/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkcsoft/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkcsoft/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkcsoft/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkcsoft/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkcsoft/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkcsoft/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkcsoft/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkcsoft/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/go-gitea/gitea/issues/740/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/go-gitea/gitea/issues/740/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}